Subject: [PATCH 03343/11362] [outer-loop] arc: PIECE 3 first positive --
 exploration DIVERSITY lifts first-win 1/11 -> 3/11

Diagnostic breakthrough: a random walk over salient candidates reaches first-win on 3/11 games
(r11l @201, sp80 @77, lp85 @142) vs the structured depth_first_ride explorer's 1/11 (lp85 only). The
structured explorer over-commits to ONE depth-first branch and MISSES easy wins -- r11l/sp80 are
trivially reachable randomly (r11l: 372/600 random steps post-win) but the structured explorer scored
0 in ~2000 actions. The failures split: 3 structure-missed (recoverable via exploration DIVERSITY) + 8
genuinely-hard (random gets 0 too -- need specific sequences). KEY: no denser reward signal exists
(frame exposes only levels_completed + win_levels=6), so this is pure sparse-reward search; diversity
is the lever for the recoverable tail. The hybrid (structured efficiency for lp85's 20-action win +
random-restart-on-stall to catch r11l/sp80) is the piece-3 deliverable. First positive result on the
0.08 wall this session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
